4|0@blackops3^1439482193#cu1p71w:gottabreathe$:I'm very disappointed by this. The VSAT is one of the primary things I've still been giddy about with the series. CoD's version of power weapons, whenever you had it, you had this rush, it's go time, I've got the power and it's time to absolutely crush, a devastating advantage. The CoD 4 Heli, the MW2 AC130, the BO1 VSAT. These were the things, when they got called in your teams said "Fuck yeah!" and the other team said "Ahhh fuck.". It's gotten harder to get these streaks, which has been a good decision, they retain their value, making those moments still mean something a decade later, but, if this is similar to the Advanced UAV, just realtime arrows, it's a little "meh". I'd prefer it taking more kills to achieve than allowing it to be shot down. Keep the wow factor.
2|0@blackops3^1439480353#cu1nzn4:TheXclusiveAce$:I'll definitely still be running it as long as it takes multiple rockets to take down. As someone that was more often on the giving end of the VSAT in BO2, I'm glad there's going to be a way to take down the HATR (as long as it takes multiple rockets and can't be taken down in seconds). While there are "sort of" counters to the VSAT, none of them are really foolproof and all of them can be negated 100% with one perk. More often than not, as soon as a VSAT is called in, several enemy players leave. I'd much rather have the enemies stay in the game and distracted with trying to shoot down my HATR than having them simply leave 2 seconds after it's called in. In addition to this, since BO2's life cycle the number of pubstomping teams (clans) seems to have increased significantly. If I'm playing solo and my teammates are feeding the enemy team of 6 organized players HATRs all game, I'd like to be able to do something about it aside from being forced to run CUAVs every game or praying for a miracle that my EMP nades will sufficiently block the mini map of the entire enemy team. Even with these sketchy counters, one thing to consider is there no longer appears to be any crutch perks in tier 2 so Hard Wired is going to be even more viable, especially if you're pubstomping and expect constant HATRs. I'm all for the HATR and I'm very excited that we have a counter to Ghost but at the same time, I'm glad it can be taken down. 
