1|0@blackops3^1439472510#cu1jgdd:peros2$:I know that not many people use hardwired, but that is also a reason why it is very hard to counter. I have often come across people running EMP and VSAT, which prevents the other team from calling in streaks to block the VSAT unless they are really lucky and have that one guy who actually uses hardwired. My first point was mainly about how weaker scorestreaks aren't often shot down, let alone the tougher ones. You do have a point about UAVs not being worth the effort though. Even so, how often are higher scorestreaks shot down? Sure, being lethal streaks makes them dangerous to face, but having your location and direction marked in realtime for your enemies also makes it dangerous to try and shoot down the HATR. You'll be stationary out in the open which makes you very vulnerable to enemies which know your exact position and direction. If it takes 3 shots to destroy, then it will probably get shot down as often as a Lodestar or Warthog. Plus, if it is really high up, then the rockets would take longer to reach it giving it extra time in the air. It would probably be almost finished by the time it does get destroyed. Overall, I don't think there is much concern about it being shot down. If Treyarch are keeping it as a high value scorestreaks, then they will make sure it is useful, while at the same time, giving it a reasonable counter that is neither too situational (having a CUAV or EMP at the right time) nor too easy.
