4|0@blackops3^1439519937#cu2cy4s:McEgan$:For people still apparently not in the know, BO2 VSAT could not be countered. If I know that it may be countered, I just wait until I die (or round change), switch classes to hardwired, and then use it. Where's your counter now? Standing still? You'll lose any game mode besides TDM if you do that. This is a good change because it brings the streak in line with all of the others. At minimum, your entire team gets the effect for as long as it takes them to shoot down. That's long enough to take control of an area or get a large boost in kills. Then, at least 1-2 people must waste 5-10 seconds shooting at it, another net gain. Even with the ability to shoot it down, you receive a large gain for using it. The fact that it can continue on for a full 45 seconds if no one attempts to shoot it is just icing that makes it even better. If it dies in 2 seconds from everyone carrying launchers, then that's still a net gain: those people essentially wasted 1/2 points to carry an item that barely sees usage, as well as having to take the time to actually shoot it. You can replace VSAT with any other large streak (swarm, dogs, chopper gunner, etc) and the same paragraph would apply to it. This change brings it down from overpowered status to being in line with every other high killstreak in the game. The only people upset over this are pubstompers that only enjoy this series as a virtual bullying simulator and hate to see their overpowered tool get taken away; the rest of us see that the change only betters the balance/gameplay.
